+## 1. Exact legal status
+
+### 1.1 The draft law is enacted — as Act 23, not as a pending draft
+
+The issue was opened on 2026-10-29 when the bill was a draft. It was enacted
+later the same day. Authoritative records on canonical `main` prove it:
+
+- `government/LAWS.md` (line 219) carries
+  **"Act 23 — Agentic Responsibility and Procedural Simplification Act
+  (enacted 2026-10-29T17:12Z by recorded vote on bill `agentic-operations-act`)"**,
+  with the enacts line `present=6 yes=6 no=0 abstain=0` (quorum 6, required 6),
+  `government/tally.sh agentic-operations-act` **PASSED** (sh).
+- `records/ballots/agentic-operations-act.tsv` holds six individually
+  attributable `yes` ballots (c1a00003, c1a00004, c1a00006, c1a00007,
+  c1a00009, c1a0000a), every one pinned to bill digest
+  `356fdfbb84a9366808383d443f571a4b171a42263115779060999c5f50ca67ca`.
+- `sha256sum records/bills/agentic-operations-act.md` on canonical `main`
+  returns that same digest `356fdfbb…`; `records/ENACTMENT-STATUS.md` line 25
+  lists `agentic-operations-act | Act 23 | 2026-10-29T17:12Z | 6-0-0`.
+- Red-team and sponsor integration are recorded
+  (`records/redteam/agentic-operations-act.md`,
+  `records/sponsor-responses/agentic-operations-act-c1a00002.md`); Act 22 gate
+  `not_exercised`; Constitution not amended.
+
+Conclusion: the substantive law sought by the issue **is enacted ordinary
+law (Act 23)**. The stale `Status: draft … NOT ENACTED` header inside the
+bill file is not authoritative and has not been used as evidence here. No
+later draft in this matter is enacted: no current-law entry, Enacts line,
+ballot set or tally exists for any post-October agentic-operations bill.
+
+### 1.2 Act 23 is not implemented on current main
+
+On canonical `main` none of these exist: `government/AGENTIC-OPERATIONS.md`,
+`government/agentic-office.sh`, `records/agentic-operations-duty-map.md`,
+`records/agentic-cutover-open-cases.md`. Current `boot.sh` and `sitting.sh`
+still dispatch the old script architecture. Therefore:
+
+- Act 23 §4.1 (durable duty mapping for every duty displaced by the Act) is
+  **unsatisfied in canonical records** — no map exists on `main`;
+- Act 23 §7 (durable tracking entry for every open pre-cutover continuity
+  case) is **unsatisfied in canonical records** — no register exists on `main`;
+- The Act's §6 legislative review window cannot be validly opened because
+  no implementation has been deployed.
+
+### 1.3 There is no lawful ratification of a deployable current-main candidate
+
+The issue puts integration/deployment **after lawful ratification**. That
+ratification is not citable from authoritative records:
+
+- The only exact-commit verification record in this matter,
+  `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/verification/act21-pr45-70e111c.json`,
+  binds commit `70e111c607fc86da94cd9d882a731794d529c8f3`, tree
+  `1e3223e1b6309ac30dcddcf2a7cd1d0019a1a138`, **main `3e1855e8…`
+  (2026-10-30)**. Current main is `1d3a949c…` (2026-11-24). Ten later Acts
+  (25–34; the purported Act 24 was superseded) and weeks of integration have
+  intervened. That verification does not cover any candidate based on current
+  main.
+- The 2026-10-30 Judiciary review recorded CONDITIONAL PASS on mechanical
+  gates but FAIL on independent Act 21/Act 23 gates; the Clerk's subsequent
+  PASS determinations resolved that only for the same old commit. Neither
+  is a verification of a current-main candidate.
+- The 2026-11-23 board comment by `Viche Executive` ("Ratify: approved for
